Ctenocystoids are likely among the most basal stem-group echinoderms.<ref name=Rahman2009/> They have also been interpreted as aberrant [[blastozoa]]ns and as stem-group [[hemichordates]].<ref name=David2000/><ref name=Dominguez2005/> The presence of stereom plates indicates that they most likely belong to the echinoderm total group, rendering a hemichordate affinity unlikely.<ref name=Rahman2009B/>

''Courtessolea'' was probably the most basal ctenocystoid, given its anatomical similarities to ''Ctenoimbricata'' and cinctans.<ref name=Zamora2012/> ''Conollia'' and ''Jugoszovia'' may be closely related to each other, as both have a reduced marginal frame compared to other ctenocystoids.<ref name=Rahman2015/>

